    "lore": "Iraq is a curious case among the motley despots and colonialists within the Italian sphere. As the Italian attempt to integrate it as a puppet state of the empire failed miserably after a revolution, Rome was forced to accept Baghdad's autonomy, and Iraq is now one of the few truly democratic states in the Middle East, at least nominally. It operates as an authoritarian democracy, in which every willing political party under the sun is allowed a foot in the government so long as they don't challenge Italian control over the nation's oil, or the political dominance of Abd al-Karim Qasim and the National Democratic Party. But the system is a house of cards, with schemers, conspirators and plotters from every direction threatening Iraq and its leader. If (or when) it all comes tumbling down, who will rise from the ashes?"
  },
